<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laufilitonga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laufilitonga was the last Tuʻi Tonga, the sacred paramount chief of Tonga. During the civil wars of the early 19th century he was defeated in 1826 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-tupou-i">Tāufaʻāhau</a>, the future King George Tupou I, who went on to unite the islands under his own rule. He lived on with sacred rank but little power, and after his death in 1865 the ancient title of Tuʻi Tonga was not renewed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laufilitonga.jpg" alt="Laufilitonga" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tauʻolunga · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laufilitonga_cross.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
